Z||000000||Richard Parnell||02-29-2000||06:57 PM||||I've been having problems with the search function, so I'll just ask.  I need the thread to repair of cracked fascias.  I've seen this discussed before. I also would like to know which rear fascia to put on my '87 coupe to accomodate dual exhausts. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||02-29-2000||08:07 PM||||My 87 SE has the dual tailpipes even though it's a four cylinder. I think any of the "aero" tails from 86-87 SE or 85 GTs. Maybe even all the other GT cars too, I'm not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||03-01-2000||01:44 PM||||The 87 and 88 coupe and the 88 Formula had basically the same facia. The 88 Formula definitely has the dual exhaust. I have heard the 88 coupe did also. <P>Looking at my 88 Formula it looks like the lower "skirt" part that has the opening for the exhaust is actually 3 separate pieces that attach to the facia. You might want to look at yours and see if the lower part can be removed from the facia. If so, you might only need those parts rather than the whole facia.||||reg||1
